==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|lecture|er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛkt͡ʃəɹɚ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛktʃəɹə/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lecturer.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A person who gives [[lecture]]s, especially as a [[profession]].
# A member of a [[university]] or [[college]] below the [[rank]] of [[assistant professor]] or [[reader]]; [[docent]]; lector.
# {{lb|en|.dated}} A member of the [[Church of England]] [[clergy]] whose main task was to deliver [[sermon]]s (''[[lecture]]s'') in the afternoons and evenings.

====Derived terms====
* [[senior lecturer]]
* [[visiting lecturer]]

